#: patterns/footer-centered-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Footer Centered — Dark"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-centered-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Dark-surface take on the centered, typographic footer. For dark campaign pages that need a closing mark rather than a set of links."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-centered.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Footer Centered"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-centered.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Centered footer with the site title stacked above two short lines of text. Deliberately typographic rather than navigational - suits single-page sites and campaign landing pages with nowhere to link."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-columns-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Footer with Nav Columns — Dark"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-columns-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Dark-surface take on the three-column sitemap footer. The usual choice for a dark site that still needs full link wayfinding beneath the content."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-columns.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Footer with Nav Columns"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-columns.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Full sitemap footer with the site logo and tagline beside two columns of grouped navigation links, over a copyright line. The most substantial footer - use it when the site has enough sections to need wayfinding at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-minimal-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Footer Minimal — Dark"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-minimal-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Dark-surface take on the compact single-row footer. Closes a dark page without the abrupt light block a default footer would leave at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-minimal.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Footer Minimal"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/footer-minimal.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Compact single-column footer with the site title, one inline link row and a copyright line. The lightest footer - best where a full sitemap would be more structure than the content warrants."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-banner-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Header with Banner — Dark"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-banner-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Dark-surface take on the two-tier header with an announcement bar. Suits dark sites running a standing notice that should stay legible without introducing a bright band at the very top."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-banner.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Header with Banner"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-banner.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Two-tier header with a full-width announcement bar above the logo and navigation row. Use it for launch notices, shipping cut-offs or a temporary promotion that needs to sit above everything without displacing the menu."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-buttons-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Header with Buttons — Dark"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-buttons-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Dark-surface take on the header with two call-to-action buttons. For dark-themed sites where the buttons should sit on an inverted bar instead of a light strip across the top of the page."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-buttons.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Header with Buttons"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-buttons.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Single-row header pairing logo and navigation with two call-to-action buttons on the right. The standard marketing header - reach for it when the site has a primary conversion action such as a signup or demo request."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-navs-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Header with Navs — Dark"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-navs-dark.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Dark-surface take on the lean logo-and-navigation header. Use it when the page opens on a dark hero and the header should read as part of that surface rather than a separate light band."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-navs.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Header with Navs"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-navs.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Single-row header with the site logo and one inline navigation menu. The leanest header in the set - use it for content sites and one-page layouts where the top of the page should stay quiet."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-woo.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "WooCommerce Header"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/header-woo.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Single-row store header with logo, navigation, a mini cart and a customer account link. For WooCommerce sites that need cart and account access on every page."
msgstr ""

